248
00:26:22,410 --> 00:26:29,590
 1939, to the amazement of the French, English, and Polish, Stalin signed a pact of non-aggression with Hitler, which left Poland wide open to him.

249
00:26:30,220 --> 00:26:33,560
 And eight days later, on the 1st of September, war.

250
00:26:34,380 --> 00:26:35,360
 Poland is invaded.

251
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:51,110
 61 nations, 100 million enlisted men would fight in the war.

252
00:26:52,210 --> 00:26:52,670
 War dead?

253
00:26:53,120 --> 00:26:54,420
 More than 50 million.

254
00:26:58,500 --> 00:27:08,060
 10 million civilians, women, children, old people exterminated in the Nazi concentration camps, defying all humanity in the name of hatred.

255
00:27:08,940 --> 00:27:10,960
 The Enola Gay flies towards Hiroshima.

256
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:22,000
 What victory?

257
00:27:22,000 --> 00:27:24,040
 What victory?

258
00:27:24,040 --> 00:27:26,040
 Europe, the cradle of humanity, is no longer.

259
00:27:26,040 --> 00:27:32,020
 In February 1945 at Yalta, what were to be the main lines of peace were drawn up.

260
00:27:32,020 --> 00:27:32,930
 A shaky peace.

261
00:27:32,930 --> 00:27:35,010
 It was based on a balance of terror.

262
00:27:35,010 --> 00:27:40,750
 And what of man in all this?

263
00:27:40,750 --> 00:27:44,450
 Man, barely able to stand on his own two legs.

